## Exclusions, era, uncertainty

**Excluded:** none of these five. No `crossing_undatable`.

**Pre-1995 hits:** **0 of 5.** All five crossings sit in 2008–2018.

**Every place I was uncertain**

1. **ARR vs GAAP** on PagerDuty and Optimizely. Same convention as Gusto/Zapier in this dataset; S-1 GAAP for PagerDuty only starts at FY2018 ($79.6M).
2. **Optimizely “double-digit millions”** is a floor. If it meant barely $10M, the 2013 margin is 38% — flagged, not under 20%.
3. **Stripe’s €14.2M is SPEL, not consolidated Stripe.** Used as a floor. Global 2014 was almost certainly larger; I did not infer how much.
4. **Patrick Collison a2** is a real gap. MIT was not completed; Leaving Cert year is not in any source I could open.
5. **WePay and Mixpanel 9-year bounds** rest on a single later $100M print plus founding year. Honest, not tight. Private-company early P&L was not found after two genuine attempts each.
6. **a3=a4 judgment calls** on Collison and Clerico (Blakely / p01 rule). A stricter reading would put those a3 cells at `unknown`.
7. **Age-derived births** (Solomon 1982-1983, Clerico 1984-1985, Doshi 1988) are not calendar-year birth records.

**Researched 5 of 5 assigned people.** No suspected fabricated roster entries. All five list memberships confirmed on a page that names the person or company.
